        "text": "You are reviewing one task's implementation: spec compliance first, then code quality. Task-scoped gate, not a merge review.\n\n## What Was Requested\n\nRead the task brief: /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-8-brief.md\n\nGlobal constraints from the spec that bind this task:\n- One EventClient per process, one SessionSender per session; the library stamps event_id (vendor_record_id wins, else uuid5), seq starting at 1 monotonic per session, event_ts (EventIn.event_ts or now), collected_ts.\n- register(): idempotent via state file (~ path from config); network call only when state file absent; persists with chmod 0600; RegistrationError on non-200, no auto-retry.\n- flush(timeout_s) passes through to Shipper.drain as total-budget deadline; close() stops flusher thread, flushes best-effort, closes shipper.\n- Auto-flush thread only when flush_interval_s > 0; must never die silently (catch, log warning).\n- structlog module field; no event content in logs.\n- Commit messages never mention Claude/AI, no Co-Authored-By lines.\n\n## What the Implementer Claims They Built\n\nRead the implementer's report: /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/task-8-report.md\n\n## Diff Under Review\n\n**Base:** 4d02997\n**Head:** 78064eb\n**Diff file:** /Users/sumandra/projects/talium/code-econ/.superpowers/sdd/review-4d02997..78064eb.diff\n\nRead the diff file once — it is your view of the change. Do not re-run git commands; do not crawl the codebase; inspect outside the diff only for a concrete named risk, one focused check per risk, named in the report. Read-only review — do not mutate the working tree, index, HEAD, or branch state.\n\n## Do Not Trust the Report\nVerify claims against the diff; rationales never downgrade findings.\n\n## Tests\nImplementer ran tests with TDD evidence; do not re-run to confirm. Focused test only for a specific doubt. Warnings/noise in reported output are findings.\n\n## Part 1: Spec Compliance\nMissing / Extra / Misunderstood. ⚠️ for anything unverifiable from the diff.\n\n## Part 2: Code Quality\nQuality (edge cases: concurrent SessionSenders sharing the spool; flusher thread lifecycle/shutdown ordering in close(); state file corruption), tests (real behavior), structure. Evidence: file:line for every finding/check.\n\nFinal message is the report itself: begin with the spec-compliance verdict; every line is a verdict, finding with file:line, or check you ran.\n\n## Calibration\nImportant = cannot be trusted until fixed. Coverage-breadth/polish = Minor. Plan-mandated defects are findings (labeled plan-mandated). Strengths first.\n\n## Output Format\n\n### Spec Compliance\n- ✅ | ❌ | ⚠️\n\n### Strengths\n### Issues\n#### Critical (Must Fix)\n#### Important (Should Fix)\n#### Minor (Nice to Have)\n\n### Assessment\n**Task quality:** [Approved | Needs fixes]\n**Reasoning:** [1-2 sentences]",
